  This is the Benson's house. The postman is putting a letter in the letterbox. 
Here's a letter for you, Jim. Ann wants Jim to open the letter quickly. Hurry up! Open it! When are they coming? 
  Dear Jim and Peggy
  Thanks for your invitation to stay at your new house. Sue is looking forward to seeing Ann.Our plane arrives at 8 o'clock on Thursday next week. It's flight number 412. Can you meet us at the airport? Looking forward to seeing you all. 
  Sincerely
  Kim. 
  Thursday next week. We can meet them at the airport, can't we? Yes, of course. I'll ring them. Thursday arrives. Lay the table, please, Ann. I'll make the toast. Butter the toast, please, Tom. Pass the milk, please, Ann.Clear the table, load the dishwasher, and let's go. It's a quarter to eight. We're early.It's half past eight. Where are Kim and Sue?
